sched/fair: track idle CPUs with a per-LLC bitmap

select_idle_cpu() capped a linear walk of the LLC. Keep a per-LLC idle
cpumask on sched_domain_shared, set and cleared with atomic bitops from
the idle class enter/exit path, and consult it from select_idle_cpu()
after the fast target/prev/recent_used_cpu candidates miss.

SIS_UTIL's overloaded early-out, the SMT idle-core walk, asym capacity
selection, and asym packing load-balance are unchanged. If the bitmap
is empty or stale, select_idle_cpu() falss back to the old walk.

Not compile-tested: no kernel config on this tree, and a full x86 build
was not run.

